{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Sorry we're late, doc. The robot by the garage was hectic and the bakkie wouldn't start. Ag, shame.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Sit. What's the problem.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): His sister phoned last night. She's on that biotin for her hair, she's not ill herself, and she reckoned his eyes look funny so we must come in.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (PATIENT): Ja, um, that's why I'm here. My eyes have gone yellow, my pee is dark like Coke, and I'm so tired. Is it serious, doc?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): When did it start.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (PATIENT): After we ate at those roadside stalls, on the trip up the coast. About ten days... no, wait, err, it was two weeks back. Ja, two weeks.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Belly pain.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (PATIENT): No. No pain. Just the yellow, the tiredness and the dark pee. Do I need hospital?",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Three of the others on that trip were ill as well, hey. The runs, and feeling rubbish. Not family, just the group from work.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you drink.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): No. I don't drink, not at all. Is it the food then? I'm really worried.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Itching. Any fever.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (PATIENT): No fever. Um, a bit of itching on my arms, ja. Does that mean the liver? My cousin had hepatitis years ago and I can't stop thinking it's the same.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pale stools.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (PATIENT): No, they're normal. Ordinary colour. What tests will you do? Can you tell me today?",
  "[SEG0016] person_4 (NURSE): Temp is 37.1 and his pulse is eighty two. I did them just now. He asked me twice if the liver is packing up.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sclerae are yellow. Abdomen soft, no tenderness. Liver edge just palpable.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): Is a palpable liver bad? I'm a panel beater, can I still go to work? Yoh, I'm anxious, hey.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He takes pain tablets for his back, the Panado. He told me seventy-five milligrams but I don't think that's right.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (PATIENT): Ag, it's paracetemol. I said seventy-five... no, it's five hundred milligrams. Two tablets when my back is sore, not every day.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Stop the paracetemol for now. Liver bloods and hepatitis serology. Nurse takes the bloods Thursday morning. Come fasting.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (PATIENT): Thursday? Must I not eat from the night before? And if the results are bad, do I get a scan? Please, I need to know.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Nothing to eat from ten the night before. If those bloods are borderline we do a third test, the viral PCR. If it does not settle, a scan of the liver. I'll see you in two weeks.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (NURSE): I'll book Thursday morning at the lab. Fasting from ten. Bring your ID.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (PATIENT): Should I take my sister's biotin too? She swears by it. And this tiredness, is the liver packing up? Will the yellow go away?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Don't take her biotin. Not your medicine. Looks like hepatitis. Provisional, mind. Could be that roadside food. Tiredness fits the jaundice.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The cousin's hepatitis was years back, he just panics about it. And he hasn't touched a drink, I can say that.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (PATIENT): Ok. Thursday, nothing from ten, and back in two weeks. If I go more yellow before then, do I come earlier? I'm scared, hey.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): If you get worse, come back sooner. Otherwise two weeks. That's it.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (PATIENT): Sharp. Thanks, doc. I'll be here Thursday. Sorry again about the bakkie."
 ],
